    Url= {http://www2.eecs.berkeley.edu/Pubs/TechRpts/2024/EECS-2024-215.html},
    Number= {UCB/EECS-2024-215},
    Abstract= {This manual describes the Saturn Vector Unit, a parameterized and extensible vector microarchitecture executing the RISC-V vector extension. Saturn was developed to address an academic need for a representative, compliant, and flexible generator of RISC-V vector units targeting deployment in domain-specialized cores. Saturn is implemented as a parameterized Chisel RTL generator, enabling a range of possible Saturn configurations across many target deployment scenarios. This document discusses the microarchitectural details of all Saturn components.},
}

